        </ul>

        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 rounded-2xl p-8 text-gray-200">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="mb-4">
            Tire marks on fresh sealer are almost always a soft coating meeting a pivoting tire, usually on a hot day, usually within the first week or two. Lighter scuffs fade on their own in a month. Black smears scrub off with soap and water. Only marks that expose asphalt or have not blended after several weeks need a thin, feathered touch-up.
          </p>
          <p class="m-0">
            Next time, apply thin, add sand, wait 48 to 72 hours before parking in summer, and keep the car rolling while you turn the wheel. If the coating is still tacky after a week or is lifting in sheets, the tire is not the problem; the application was, and that is a different repair.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>
